  "confidence": 0.85,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D4", "D14", "D23"],
      "pins": ["D4.2", "D14.2", "D23.2"],
      "nets": ["/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW"],
      "observed": "The net /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW contains only the anodes of D4, D14, and D23; it has no connection to +3V3, a switched supply, a driver, or any other source.",
      "expected": "A net named LED_3.3V_POWER_SW should be connected to a 3.3 V power source (or a switched 3.3 V source) so that the LEDs can light; the LED cathodes are tied to active-low signal nets, implying the anode side must be powered.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW\") ... (node (ref \"D14\") (pin \"2\") ... (node (ref \"D23\") (pin \"2\") ... (node (ref \"D4\") (pin \"2\") ..."},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"D1\") (pin \"2\") ..."}
      ],
      "impact": "D4, D14, and D23 will remain dark; Ethernet/activity LED indication intended by the board will not work.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R28"],
      "pins": ["R28.1", "R28.2"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "SCL0_GPIO45"],
      "observed": "R28 is a pull-up from +3V3 to SCL0_GPIO45, but its schematic value is 10 and the SPICE deck models it as 10 ohms, while its own description/MPN/LCSC fields identify a 10k resistor.",
      "expected": "I2C pull-ups on this board are normally 10k (e.g. R23, R29, R30), and a 10-ohm pull-up is not a valid I2C pull-up value.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R28\") (value \"10\") ... (description \" 100mW Thick Film Resistors 75V ±100ppm/℃ ±1% 10kΩ 0603 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") (value \" 0603WAF1002T5E\"))"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "R28 +3V3 SCL0_GPIO45 10"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"R28\") (pin \"1\") ..."}
      ],
      "impact": "SCL0 would be driven through an excessively strong 10-ohm pull-up, preventing normal I2C low states and potentially causing excessive current on the I2C0 bus.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U10", "U11"],
      "pins": ["U10.4", "U10.5", "U11.4", "U11.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "Both GND1 and GND2 pins of the isolated CAN transceivers U10 and U11 are connected to the same GND net.",
      "expected": "For isolated CAN buses, the logic-side ground (GND1) and bus-side ground (GND2) should be separate/isolated; the specification states the board implements two isolated CAN buses.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"80\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") ... (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") ... (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") ... (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") ..."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (`U8`, `U9`) through an isolated CAN transceiver"}
      ],
      "impact": "The galvanic isolation between the CM4 logic side and the CAN bus side is defeated, so the CAN interfaces are not truly isolated as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The files contain at least two clear deviations: a floating 3.3 V LED power net leaving D4/D14/D23 unpowered, and R28 being modeled as a 10-ohm I2C pull-up instead of 10k. The isolated CAN transceiver grounds also appear tied together, which contradicts the intended isolated CAN buses."
}

